      "writtenOn": "2026-08-19T20:24:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, this is an implementation that could land on the main branch. The \"ABI Compliance\" part would need to be added to the allowed_breaks file to clear the change. I suppose we could also just land it here but this is not a KMI breaking patch.\n\n\u003e I\u0027m still mystified why the fscrypt structs need to be stable at all. We do not support vendor modules using them. It makes no sense.\n\nInteresting, I wonder why it was added to the STG monitoring file then. I\u0027ll have a quick look.",
      "parentUuid": "1cb51e13_5b574e04",
      "revId": "786c76c6bcad2ed54c8549a59780221c2ec8208e",
